## Important Logical Constraint

Do NOT report a tree merely because

```
n2 < 2q - 1.
```

It is a counterexample ONLY if its exact burning number also satisfies

```
b(T) > q.
```

For example, a tree with n=14 has

```
q = ceil(sqrt(14)) = 4,
```

not q=3.

Therefore a tree with n2=0 and b(T)=4 is NOT a counterexample.

